# WORLD project guidance

- Treat `WORLD.md` and `docs/philosophy.md` as the agent/tool guidance; skill wrappers point there.
- `WORLD.md` is the world only (cast, relations, vocabulary, scope in the world's words): it is
  sent with every mention turn. Commands, paths, schedules, and current state go in `README.md`,
  `settings.json`, or the generated `STATUS.md`.
- Treat `world/`, `bin/`, `docs/`, `templates/`, and `.codex/hooks/` as kit-owned; fix the source kit and
  rerun the installer instead of forking installed copies. If the kit fails on this machine,
  fix the minimum in `world/`, list it in a note outside `world/`, and report it upstream;
  never add a `kit-source/` checkout or a `patches/` pipeline to the harness.
- `project-profile.json` records the OS, runtime, and channel this harness was installed for;
  keep `harness.py` within it, and re-run the installer with a flag to change it.
- Agent authority comes from `Agent.tools`, scoped handler closures, read-only sandboxing,
  and generated `.the-world/agent-scope.json`, never from prompt promises.
- Outward side effects require the existing one-shot approval gate.
- A successful process is not completion when an agent promises a report; verify the
  expected file exists.
- Scheduled workers finish with a summary a person can read, rather than "done" or
  "saved report.md". `Agent(announce="result")` shows that final message in the card;
  `announce="evidence"` shows the completion check, and `announce="file"` (needs
  `writes_report=True`) shows the report's opening: front matter and a leading `# `
  title are skipped, then up to the first `## ` (the first section, if that comes next).
  Put the summary first in the report for `file`, and keep a readable final message for
  its fallback. Other values are rejected when the Agent is constructed.
- `file` picks from this attempt's files in that task's `work/` (its artifacts, and files
  modified since the attempt was claimed), not older reports (judged by modification time). `announce_file="briefing.md"`
  (a path or glob under `work/`) names the report; otherwise `.md`, then `.txt`, top level
  first, skipping hidden files, logs, and data. It tries them in order and reads at most
  64 KiB of regular, single-linked UTF-8 text; when none is usable, `result` is shown.
  The best 500 matches are retained after filtering/ranking; discovery still walks the
  tree. Claims record nanoseconds, but preserved mtimes and clock changes can affect
  this time-based selection. Files are opened from a pinned work-directory fd,
  rejecting symlinks at every component and all multiply linked files. Platforms
  without safe descriptor-relative opens show `result`. On native Windows `file` never
  shows a report: every card falls back to `result`, with no warning when the Agent
  starts, so use `result` there.
  All modes keep the channel's normal card limits and mention handling. File excerpts
  additionally mask provider tokens, named credentials and whole secret env values;
  result, evidence and error masking keep their existing behavior. Masking cannot
  catch every secret: do not announce raw logs or dumps.
